### CDC Prerequisites

To use CDC with OLake Go, you must enable CDC on both the database and individual tables you want to capture.

**Note (info):**
CDC change tables retain events for **3 days** by default (configurable via `sys.sp_cdc_change_job`). Reducing retention raises the risk of losing unconsumed events during downtime; if events expire before processing, a **full backfill** is required to restore consistency. It is recommended to **increase or adjust the retention period** based on your workload and recovery requirements.

#### 1. Required Permissions

The database user must have permission to read CDC-related metadata. Grant the following depending on your SQL Server version:

```sql
USE master;
CREATE LOGIN <olake_user> WITH PASSWORD = <password>;
CREATE USER <olake_user> FOR LOGIN <olake_user>;

USE <DATABASE>;
CREATE USER <olake_user> FOR LOGIN <olake_user>;
-- The following grants access to the `dbo` schema.
-- If your tables reside in different schemas, run an equivalent GRANT statement for each.
GRANT SELECT ON SCHEMA :: dbo TO <olake_user>;
GRANT SELECT ON SCHEMA :: cdc TO <olake_user>;
GRANT VIEW DATABASE STATE TO <olake_user>;

USE msdb;
CREATE USER <olake_user> FOR LOGIN <olake_user>;
-- The following grants access to the `dbo` schema.
-- If your tables reside in different schemas, run an equivalent GRANT statement for each.
GRANT SELECT ON dbo.cdc_jobs TO <olake_user>;
```

```sql
USE master;
CREATE LOGIN <olake_user> WITH PASSWORD = <password>;
CREATE USER <olake_user> FOR LOGIN <olake_user>;

USE <DATABASE>;
CREATE USER <olake_user> FOR LOGIN <olake_user>;
-- The following grants access to the `dbo` schema.
-- If your tables reside in different schemas, run an equivalent GRANT statement for each.
GRANT SELECT ON SCHEMA :: dbo TO <olake_user>;
GRANT SELECT ON SCHEMA :: cdc TO <olake_user>;
